---
// about.astro — full about page — the practice, the person, the name
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Mathim Divisions is Cassie's clarity practice — IT work, writing, tools, and whatever comes next."
>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 160px;">
    <p class="section-label">About</p>
    <h1 class="section-heading">Hi, I'm Cassie</h1>
    <p class="section-subtitle">
      Mathim Divisions is my practice. It's the name I put on my work — whatever shape that work takes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>The Practice</h2>
    <p>
      I'm an IT technician, a writer, and someone who builds things. Mathim Divisions is
      the container for all of it. Right now, that means IT audits, documentation, and roadmaps
      for small businesses — plus a blog about technology and practice, plus digital products
      on Gumroad. Tomorrow it might be something else. The container doesn't limit the work;
      it just gives it a name.
    </p>
    <p>
      I believe small businesses deserve the same clarity as enterprises, without the enterprise
      overhead. Most IT documentation is written for other IT people. Mine is written for the
      people who run the business — the office manager, the operations director, the person who
      just needs to know where the passwords are and whether the backups ran.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>How I Work</h2>
    <p>
      I work solo, supported by good tools and a continuity-aware agent system that helps me
      produce at a level usually associated with larger firms. The output is always human —
      clear, specific, and written for the people who will actually use it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every engagement starts with listening. I don't sell software, I don't push products,
      and I don't recommend solutions until I understand the problem. The deliverable is always
      a document you can hand to anyone — your next IT hire, your compliance auditor, or yourself
      six months from now when you need to remember how something works.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>The Name</h2>
    <p>
      "Mathim" comes from childhood — a nonsense word that a friend and I invented as a pretend
      company name. Years later, I asked permission to keep it. He said yes.
    </p>
    <p>
      "Divisions" is about clarity through separation. Taking something tangled and dividing it
      into coherent parts — whether that's an IT environment, a complex idea, or a project that
      needs structure. It's the act of making something complex into something you can see.
    </p>
    <p>
      It's not "Solutions." It's not "Systems." It's divisions. The work of clarity.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
